What is Convolution?
Convolution is a mathematical operation where small filters move across an image to detect important patterns such as:
Edges
Shapes
Textures
Corners
CNNs automatically learn these filters during training.

Why is Pooling Used?
Pooling helps reduce image size while preserving important features.

Benefits:
Reduces computation
Prevents overfitting
Makes training faster
Keeps important visual information
Max pooling is commonly used in CNNs.

Why is ReLU Commonly Used?
ReLU stands for Rectified Linear Unit.
f(x)=max(0,x)

Advantages:
Faster learning
Solves vanishing gradient problem
Introduces non-linearity
Why are CNNs Better than Regular Feed-Forward Networks for Images?

CNNs are better because they:
Preserve spatial relationships
Automatically learn features
Use fewer parameters
Work efficiently on image data

Feed-forward networks flatten images and lose spatial information.
